WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.181
Question five.

00:00:01.181 --> 00:00:06.414
Step one: macro scan. It asks the information-literate action.

00:00:06.414 --> 00:00:09.283
One mark. Command words: “action”.

00:00:09.283 --> 00:00:10.802
Step two: denoise.

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:15.781
Useful, in yellow: the claim “never trust any social post”.

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:20.929
In cyan: the absolute word “all”, and “information literacy”.

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:26.330
Useless red herring: how sensational the title is — kick it out.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.849
Step three: draft.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:30.887
Literacy: verify first, judge later.

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:33.841
No blind trust, no blind rejection.

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:36.204
Check author, date, sources.

00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:37.639
Step four: P O E.

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:41.942
A, forward at once: spreads without checking — cut.

00:00:41.942 --> 00:00:46.162
B, delete without checking: blind rejection — cut.

00:00:46.162 --> 00:00:49.538
D, judge by title only: one-sided — cut.

00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:59.833
Step five: sanity check and lock. The one left checks author, date and sources before judging — exactly verify-then-judge.

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.112
So the correct answer is C.
